=head1 DESCRIPTION

Options for how to import Neptune data.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 PreserveDefaultVertexLabels => Bool

Neptune Analytics supports label-less vertices and no labels are
assigned unless one is explicitly provided. Neptune assigns default
labels when none is explicitly provided. When importing the data into
Neptune Analytics, the default vertex labels can be omitted by setting
I<preserveDefaultVertexLabels> to false. Note that if the vertex only
has default labels, and has no other properties or edges, then the
vertex will effectively not get imported into Neptune Analytics when
preserveDefaultVertexLabels is set to false.


=head2 PreserveEdgeIds => Bool

Neptune Analytics currently does not support user defined edge ids. The
edge ids are not imported by default. They are imported if
I<preserveEdgeIds> is set to true, and ids are stored as properties on
the relationships with the property name I<neptuneEdgeId>.


=head2 B<REQUIRED> S3ExportKmsKeyId => Str

The KMS key to use to encrypt data in the S3 bucket where the graph
data is exported


=head2 B<REQUIRED> S3ExportPath => Str

The path to an S3 bucket from which to import data.



